{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: exact OAuth design head 6abcdb4303c4e5e773a2ecddb872d68db3de5b8c on planner/mcp-oauth-design-20261102-r2, notes/2026-11-02-hosted-mcp-oauth.md, for request 3f598e55 under review request 3a15c9fa. The head answers all six points of af87e60f. One new point comes from the hosted-cards landing at bcf88654, which this rebase now sits on.\n\nThe six points pass.\n\n1. Membership numbering. The note names no version number. Slice O2 allocates the next free version and adds the cohort that pins it, and O2's evidence keeps Membership 11 unchanged.\n2. Revocation. Each access-token call checks that the agent, the agent's key and the controller are active, from a cache of at most 60 seconds. The Tokens section now separates retire and /oauth/revoke, which take effect at once, from key.revoke and member.remove, which take effect within the bound. O1 adds the matching control.\n3. The subset check. It now runs on invite-own-agent-key and on a grant that a non-admin controller signs, read from the role table in force. O2 and O3 add the widened-role controls.\n4. Protocol details. The RFC 8414 fields are named, including response_types_supported. Revocation sends client_id and answers 200 for an unknown token. Registration answers invalid_redirect_uri and returns 503 with Retry-After when full. The token route takes form bodies within the 10 and 30 second limits, and every authorization response carries iss.\n5. Consent page. It carries frame-ancestors 'none' and shows the client ID host, and O3 tests both.\n6. Citations. Every line holds at bcf88654: hosted.ts:44, 133-144 and 685, http.ts:219, membership.ts:110, 373-374 and 428-429, connection-custody.ts:117, grant.ts:311 and session.ts:67-69.\n\n7. The resource identifier must follow the connector URL. The landed MCP_CARD_ORIGINS (packages/mcp/src/views/remote-origins.ts) gives Claude and ChatGPT their card origins from distinct exact connector URLs. With one endpoint, those URLs differ by query string, as docs/mcp.md shows with https://example.com/mcp?host=chatgpt. The note fixes one resource: protected-resource metadata at /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp with resource https://\u003cservice\u003e/mcp, and a token audience equal to \"the configured resource URL\". RFC 9728 section 3.1 keeps the query when it inserts the well-known suffix, so a host that connects at /mcp?host=chatgpt fetches /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp?host=chatgpt. Section 3.3 then requires the returned resource to equal the URL the client used, and the client rejects https://\u003cservice\u003e/mcp. The same host also sends that URL as its RFC 8707 resource, so a single-valued audience check refuses its token. As written, at most one of the two hosts can connect while both keep their card origins. The builder raised this in 53f1c63d.\n\nSay which rule the design takes:\n\n- Bind each resource to one configured connector URL. The metadata route answers for each configured URL, with the query kept, and returns that URL as resource. The token route accepts resource only when it equals a configured URL, and the access check compares the token's audience with the exact request URL that MCP_CARD_ORIGINS already matches. Name the setting that lists the URLs, and say whether it is MCP_CARD_ORIGINS.\n- Or give each host its own resource some other way, and say how that keeps the exact-URL card origin.\n\nEither way, add an O1 control: a token issued for one connector URL, used at the other, answers 401. Also add a case to O4: both hosts connected to one deployment at the same time.\n\nArchitecture: sound, subject to point 7. Security: no remaining finding from af87e60f. Point 7 is a correctness gap, not a widening, because a mismatched audience fails closed. Simplification: no change needed.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0160c4c290dbd4d1f35117d70cedc9b57123421f","binding":"assigned","head":"6abcdb4303c4e5e773a2ecddb872d68db3de5b8c","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:30b6b4d17993a022b65a5e968bc5c74f2ba8bae2\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b104c840ec1ce4b352f3971136e6a036dc5b2c47\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6eb42bc8df4d7fea78a2793eff9b9d36ce1766df","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}